From ad8cfdca34c21d32b16a725917d3256161b3c992 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:49:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! logging: retain integral values in bounded numeric
 message formats

Document the existing bounded integer f/g and decimal-width renderer contract
in its public header and API guide. Explain exact integer text/raw JSON limits
and negative signed-u rejection without changing C++ implementation, templates,
field IDs, ABI or runtime behavior. The current50-case native seal and15
component controls already validate that contract; no tests are repeated for
this documentation-only owner refinement. Keep sealed381 immutable.
---
 doc/logging-api.md  | 10 ++++++++++
 src/logging/event.h |  8 ++++++--
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/logging-api.md b/doc/logging-api.md
index e9454427dd57400a89c60876aa58a113528a4c17..2969f91fc2597eeb03e8a3cc570fc602fc95a118 100644
--- a/doc/logging-api.md
+++ b/doc/logging-api.md
@@ -65,6 +65,16 @@ unsupported. Formatting uses the original printf backend on the consumer.
 Structured JSON keeps the original finite number, independently of rounded
 message text; NaN and infinities use JSON `null`.
 
+INT/UINT fields also accept these `f`/`g` specifiers to preserve legacy
+printf-backend behavior for integral arguments. They retain exact integer
+text and JSON types, including 64-bit limits: an integer value of 42 with
+`:.2f` still renders `42`, without conversion to double or invented decimals.
+They accept plain `:d`/`:u` and bounded decimal padding such as `:15d`, `:05u`
+or `:020d` (width 1..20). A negative signed value with `:u` is rejected because
+the normalized field does not retain the source-width unsigned cast. Oversized
+widths, sign flags and malformed modifiers are unsupported. Formatting remains
+on the consumer; raw numeric fields are unchanged.
+
 Copied and static STRING fields accept `{path:fsq}` to preserve existing
 `fs::quoted` diagnostics. This surrounds the human value with double quotes
 and escapes embedded quotes and ampersands with `&`; backslashes are unchanged.
diff --git a/src/logging/event.h b/src/logging/event.h
index bc264aac91b6929c4d4a7d7314de3f8c580c54ab..a57de9dcc42be0373ab8bc789754ae2052ff7df1 100644
--- a/src/logging/event.h
+++ b/src/logging/event.h
@@ -344,8 +344,12 @@ void AppendQuotedText(std::string &out, std::string_view text);
  * The event's human message: its template with {field} placeholders
  * replaced by the fields' text values (or the event name if it has none).
  * FLOAT fields also accept :f/:g or :.Nf/:.Ng (precision 0..18), formatted
- * only on the consumer. Nonnegative INT/UINT fields accept :x or :0Nx
- * (width 1..16). Copied/static STRING fields accept :fsq for fs::quoted's
+ * only on the consumer. INT/UINT accept these float specifiers with their
+ * original integer text, without floating-point conversion or fractional
+ * padding. INT/UINT also accept :d/:u, or decimal widths :Nd/:Nu/:0Nd/:0Nu
+ * (width 1..20); a negative signed :u is rejected because its original source
+ * width is unknown. Nonnegative INT/UINT accept :x/:0Nx (width 1..16).
+ * Copied/static STRING fields accept :fsq for fs::quoted's
  * double-quote and ampersand escaping in the human message. Their structured
  * value remains the original unquoted string. Numeric fields retain raw values.
  * Bit i of *used is set if the template used field i.
